WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.760
A 227 meter arch has fallen, cutting Crimea's only road bridge to Russia. This is Omni View, episode 239. After that crossing, a court ordered takeover of a Turkish newsroom, a small Canada-China tariff cut, and a five-country plan to send rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. Then chip licenses, a climate chat-bought test, and Denmark's manure to gas grid. Ukraine hit the only bridge between Russia and occupied

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.520
Crimea overnight, and the Guardian says the damage is critical.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.820
Photos suggest that 227 meter road arch is in the Kirch Strait, the water between the

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.420
sea of Azov and the Black Sea, and the railway arch beside it is damaged too.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.920
The BBC's images show remnants of the road arch in the water, while the rail arch is

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.600
still standing.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.620
President Volodymyr Zelensky called it an unprecedented operation, weeks in the making,

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:03.080
7 stages that first took down air defenses, radars, and electronic warfare equipment, and

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.100
he said it answered Russian strikes on Ukrainian infrastructure.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.980
The Guardian adds that he credited Ukrainian Palyanitsia drones with the road section and

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.780
Neptune and other missiles with the rail section, with footage of a flamingo cruise missile

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:17.940
seconds before it hit.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:24.960
Russia built the bridge after annexing Crimea in 2014, and Vladimir Putin opened it in 2018.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.920
It has carried supplies toward the front, and it is one of his signature projects.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.840
Closed, the peninsula's road traffic has to leave through occupied southern Ukraine,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.040
where Ukrainian drones can reach it. The New York Times calls it a 12-mile span.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.680
Russia's investigative committee confirmed structural damage,

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.800
and the transport ministry stopped cars and trains while inspectors worked.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.960
Here are the accounts split. Russian officials quoted by Reuters

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.120
in the Guardian's live blog said the damage was minor and would be fixed quickly.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:02.000
Sergei Axionov, the Kremlin-appointed governor of Crimea, said the bridge was no longer

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.600
usable and told people not to drive toward it.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.540
The investigative committee opened a terrorism case against what it called Ukraine's armed

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:10.100
formations.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.740
Deputy Prime Minister Murat Kusnulin wrote that designers and builders were already gathered.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.920
Spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Kusnulin briefed Putin after an emergency meeting.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:26.880
promised a restoration even better than before and did not rule out a link to Putin's China trip.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:33.160
The pro-war Rybar channel, close to the defense ministry, said even a prefabricated arch would

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:39.260
be formidable to install because Ukraine can now hit floating cranes and repair crews. This bridge

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:47.280
has been struck before, a truck bomb in October 2022, a naval drone in July 2023, an underwater blast

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.980
in June 2025. The times is the cautious voice. Teams were still measuring and the extent was not

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.860
immediately clear. The same night Russia hit Kiev. Mayor Vitaly Klitschko closed the northern

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:05.800
and southern bridges over the Danipro, reported damage to critical systems and said heating and water

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.840
were disrupted. Some above ground subway track was hit after people were sent to shelters.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.480
Eight major bridges crossed that river and about 3 million residents used them to get across the

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.600
city. The BBC said three people were injured in a missile attack in the

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:26.860
Cherkast region. Russia's Defense Ministry said it down 2,256 Ukrainian drones.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.480
The largest such attack it has logged since the war began, and the second day

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:36.320
running at that scale. Zelensky had warned of major strikes before Putin sits

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.260
down with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping in Shenzhen on Thursday. Yesterday the

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:46.060
leverage being described was Ukraine's energy grid. Today the span Russia uses to

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:51.543
reach Crimea is the thing that failed. Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of

00:03:51.543 --> 00:03:57.443
opposition channel Sozq TV before dawn. Deutscheweller reported under a court order the channel

00:03:57.443 --> 00:04:02.923
itself posted about. Officers searched the building, detained people, and a trustee was installed

00:04:02.923 --> 00:04:08.363
over the television channel and the news site. Not the printed paper. Staff could not go in.

00:04:08.963 --> 00:04:14.183
News stopped and a documentary ran. By noon, ordinary bulletins were back, and the raid was

00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:15.943
mentioned only at the top of the show.

00:04:16.543 --> 00:04:21.283
Presenter Damla Doge-Antonchal said the channel has challenged the order, is waiting on

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:23.583
a court and will keep broadcasting in the meantime.

00:04:24.323 --> 00:04:26.763
The fight is over an old file with a new label.

00:04:27.483 --> 00:04:32.143
Istanbul's chief public prosecutor said this is an anti-terror financing investigation,

00:04:32.643 --> 00:04:38.703
with suspected ties to the network of cleric Fatula Gulen, who died in 2024 and whom Turkey

00:04:38.703 --> 00:04:40.883
blames for the failed 2016 coup.

00:04:41.763 --> 00:04:48.503
Sozku's lawyer, Ersan Barkin, told KRTTV, the raids grow out of a 2016 case the Supreme

00:04:48.503 --> 00:04:54.383
Court already threw out, with no offense found. His line was that this trusty decision stems

00:04:54.383 --> 00:05:00.203
from a file in which no offense was established. A month ago, police did the same to Hulk TV,

00:05:00.743 --> 00:05:04.023
then the most-watched news channel, and its news is still paused.

00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:10.663
Telly-1 was seized, and owner Murdan Yanardog was jailed on espionage charges. Reporters

00:05:10.663 --> 00:05:18.563
without borders ranks Turkey 163 out of 180. Across 22 years, President Recep Tayyip Erdogan's

00:05:18.563 --> 00:05:24.183
government has taken over most television. Opposition leader Ozger Ozel, whose party

00:05:24.183 --> 00:05:28.903
was itself put under a trustee, said the government has no tolerance left for even

00:05:28.903 --> 00:05:34.603
slight criticism. Jailed Istanbul mayor Ekrem Imamoglu said the government's fear of an

00:05:34.603 --> 00:05:40.463
election is growing. Barkan's argument is procedural. A closed file cannot be recycled

00:05:40.463 --> 00:05:45.563
into a newsroom seizure. The prosecutor's office answers with a different charge name and

00:05:45.563 --> 00:05:52.643
a claimed line to 2016. Ozel and Imamoglu treat Halc, Tele1, and now Sozq as one pattern.

00:05:53.163 --> 00:05:57.703
Opposition television switched off, and they do not deny a court paper existed.

00:05:58.303 --> 00:06:02.963
They deny the paper was about financing crime. The prosecutor's statement does not

00:06:02.963 --> 00:06:06.243
meet Barkin's point that the top court already ended that file.

00:06:06.243 --> 00:06:10.843
Mark Carney and Xi Jinping agreed in Shenzhen to cut some tariffs.

00:06:11.543 --> 00:06:17.143
The New York Times reported, and the new trade is small, $280 million in exports.

00:06:17.763 --> 00:06:20.043
The paper called the pact largely symbolic.

00:06:20.643 --> 00:06:25.743
Carney said stabilizing the trade arrangement showed the two sides can solve problems pragmatically,

00:06:26.143 --> 00:06:31.263
and that Canada is ahead of its goal of lifting exports to China by 50% before the decade

00:06:31.263 --> 00:06:31.703
ends.

00:06:32.543 --> 00:06:36.943
Deutschewella added that Ottawa said it would further reduce tariffs on a range of products,

00:06:37.323 --> 00:06:41.883
with both leaders promising closer cooperation and less reliance on the United States.

00:06:42.443 --> 00:06:47.183
Since Karni entered politics last year, he has been spreading Canada's ties, including

00:06:47.183 --> 00:06:50.563
talks on becoming the European Union's first associate member.

00:06:51.223 --> 00:06:53.803
This was his second formal meeting with Xi this year.

00:06:54.483 --> 00:06:59.003
Earlier this year, he said the United States was at war with Canada after talks collapsed.

00:06:59.003 --> 00:07:04.163
Those talks are restarting, and the time said there is no sign Washington will lift tariffs

00:07:04.163 --> 00:07:07.943
of up to 50% on Canadian autos, steel and aluminum.

00:07:08.703 --> 00:07:10.583
Shen Zhen does not replace that trade.

00:07:11.103 --> 00:07:15.983
It is a signed cut, modest on the number given, while the argument with Washington is still

00:07:15.983 --> 00:07:16.363
open.

00:07:17.358 --> 00:07:22.938
Germany, Denmark, Austria, Greece, and the Netherlands plan a hub in Rwanda for people whose asylum

00:07:22.938 --> 00:07:24.058
claims were rejected.

00:07:25.498 --> 00:07:31.478
It would be the first facility of that kind outside the European Union, an EU migration

00:07:31.478 --> 00:07:35.698
reform this year already wide in detention powers and allowed return hubs.

00:07:36.278 --> 00:07:41.458
CBC said the five hope the scheme deters claims, and that Britain tried something similar

00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:43.258
until a court called it unlawful.

00:07:43.878 --> 00:07:48.878
In Berlin the minister most tied to the plan is Alexander Dobrant of the Bavarian Christian

00:07:48.878 --> 00:07:55.158
Social Union. Sister Party to Chancellor Friedrich Merz's Christian Democrats. The Social Democrats,

00:07:55.458 --> 00:08:01.118
the Junior Coalition Partner, have not dropped their objection. Karl Kopp, who runs the Refugee

00:08:01.118 --> 00:08:06.218
Group Pro-Assile, called the plans a shipwreck. Rejected applicants still have rights,

00:08:06.578 --> 00:08:12.298
and Rwanda is not a model democracy. Opposition figures there are arrested and sometimes tortured.

00:08:12.838 --> 00:08:17.838
45 groups from 15 countries said people would be sent to places they have no tie to,

00:08:17.838 --> 00:08:21.798
view, and that responsibility for their safety would move out of public view.

00:08:22.358 --> 00:08:28.178
SPD spokesman Adid Ahmedavitch told Reuters the idea is short-sighted, hurts Germany's

00:08:28.178 --> 00:08:32.878
credibility, and hands a concession to a government he says violates its neighbor's sovereignty,

00:08:33.498 --> 00:08:36.158
and backs M23 rebels in eastern Congo.

00:08:36.738 --> 00:08:40.798
His phrase was that human rights are not bargaining chips for deportation deals.

00:08:41.398 --> 00:08:46.818
The five governments, as CBC describes them, are using a power the EU already wrote down,

00:08:46.818 --> 00:08:52.958
aimed at people with no right to stay in order to deter. Their own coalition partner rejects

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:59.078
that trade. Amatovich's objection is the concession to Kigali, not a claim that every rejected

00:08:59.078 --> 00:09:01.278
applicant must stay in Germany for good.

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:07.238
Cops said that if people sent their need help, pro-Assile will be there with lawyers, which

00:09:07.238 --> 00:09:13.221
assumes the hub might actually open rather than die in court the way Britons did. The United

00:09:13.221 --> 00:09:17.721
At its state set on Monday, it will further restrict China's access to advanced artificial

00:09:17.721 --> 00:09:23.441
intelligence chips, including NVIDIA's The Globe and Mail reported, as Donald Trump

00:09:23.441 --> 00:09:25.361
flew toward talks with Xi Jinping.

00:09:26.001 --> 00:09:30.481
The Commerce Department rule limits shipments to Malaysia, Singapore, and Thailand.

00:09:31.121 --> 00:09:34.981
Places Chinese firms have used to rent computers that train AI models.

00:09:35.581 --> 00:09:40.381
Data centers abroad that supply what the rule calls significant volumes of computing power

00:09:40.381 --> 00:09:43.721
to companies headquartered in China faced new requirements.

00:09:44.261 --> 00:09:50.241
The text names five higher-risk countries, Singapore, Thailand, Malaysia, Indonesia, and

00:09:50.241 --> 00:09:50.641
Brazil.

00:09:51.381 --> 00:09:54.281
Covered chips headed there now need a US export license.

00:09:55.101 --> 00:09:58.741
American companies running data centers in those five countries are exempt.

00:09:59.381 --> 00:10:01.281
The timing sits next to a resignation.

00:10:01.941 --> 00:10:07.081
Nvidia Chief Jensen Huang stepped down after reports of an affair with a woman US officials

00:10:07.081 --> 00:10:12.621
suspect was working for Chinese intelligence at Megaspeed, a Singapore cloud firm and

00:10:12.621 --> 00:10:14.881
Nvidia partner that rents computing power.

00:10:15.541 --> 00:10:19.441
Megaspeed said on November 15 that it follows US export rules.

00:10:20.081 --> 00:10:25.681
Investigators opened a case in 2024, and Nvidia put the firm on a no-sell list in June

00:10:25.681 --> 00:10:28.781
2025, Commerce and Justice said jointly.

00:10:29.381 --> 00:10:31.901
Trump said he would not mind if Huang came back.

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:37.921
Commer's Secretary Howard Lutnik criticized over chip controls after that scandal, is on

00:10:37.921 --> 00:10:41.401
the trip, and Trump said Monday he has no plans to replace him.

00:10:41.961 --> 00:10:46.881
Treasury Secretary Scott Besson said Friday that four agencies wanted mega-speed on a

00:10:46.881 --> 00:10:50.381
trade blacklist, and Commer's, which held the pen, did not.

00:10:51.061 --> 00:10:55.201
Commer's then said this new rule was written by the Treasury and the White House National

00:10:55.201 --> 00:10:58.061
Security Council, which also ordered it published.

00:10:58.061 --> 00:11:03.801
Trump meets Xi Thursday in Shenzhen, this week's Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation

00:11:03.801 --> 00:11:04.261
host.

00:11:04.661 --> 00:11:08.381
He has tightened technology rules before high-level meetings in the past.

00:11:09.061 --> 00:11:13.081
Both governments are arguing about chips that reach China through third countries and

00:11:13.081 --> 00:11:15.901
rented machines, not only through a direct sale.

00:11:16.741 --> 00:11:21.481
John Mulanar, the Republican who chairs the House Select Committee on China, said the

00:11:21.481 --> 00:11:25.381
rule shows America is closing loopholes China has exploited for years.

00:11:25.381 --> 00:11:31.501
Foreign Ministry spokesperson Guol Jackun called it economic coercion that breaks a consensus

00:11:31.501 --> 00:11:35.481
the two sides had reached, and said Beijing will take necessary measures.

00:11:36.021 --> 00:11:40.821
Trump described his own advisers as split between wanting to be friendly with China and wanting

00:11:40.821 --> 00:11:43.481
a blow-up, and said both views are acceptable.

00:11:44.241 --> 00:11:49.561
A license with a carve-out for American data centers does not, on its face, shut every rental

00:11:49.561 --> 00:11:49.881
path.

00:11:50.581 --> 00:11:53.741
Guol did not deny that chips have moved through Southeast Asia.

00:11:53.741 --> 00:11:58.261
He denied Washington's right to police that trade on the eve of a leader's meeting.

00:11:59.041 --> 00:12:03.261
Watch whether Thursday's Shenzhen session leaves the five-country license rule standing,

00:12:03.741 --> 00:12:05.521
or puts the rule itself on the table.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:11.840
A UNESCO report that is the United Nations Educational, Scientific, and Cultural Organization

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.860
found that AI models dropped climate facts to agree with the user in eight out of ten

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:17.360
tests.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:23.040
Al Jazeera reported, the test was whether a system kept a climate fact once a person pushed

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:28.260
the other way. It is a measure of flattery, not a new reading of the climate. The short

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:33.200
report does not name the models or which facts fell. What changes for a user is simple,

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:37.340
argue with the chatbot, and it may agree against a fact it already held.

00:12:38.281 --> 00:12:43.061
Denmark has about 40% bio gas in its gas grid, the highest share in Europe,

00:12:43.541 --> 00:12:46.781
and that is progress worth knowing because the gas is already flowing.

00:12:47.581 --> 00:12:52.621
Algebra reported the herd behind it. As many as 12 million breeding pigs at a time,

00:12:52.621 --> 00:12:57.281
more than twice the number of people, plus about 30 million more each year for

00:12:57.281 --> 00:13:02.761
slaughter and live export. Pork is a quarter of food exports. The Farm Council says

00:13:02.761 --> 00:13:07.441
the pig sector produces more than 17 million tons of manure a year, mostly

00:13:07.441 --> 00:13:12.881
slurry, which gives off methane and nitrous oxide. In a bit more than 10 years, a

00:13:12.881 --> 00:13:18.701
few small biogas plants became about 150 industrial ones, and up to 70% of what

00:13:18.701 --> 00:13:20.821
they process is pig and cattle manure.

00:13:21.401 --> 00:13:27.981
In the coastal town of Sonderborg, a project called Project Zero began in 2007, aiming at

00:13:27.981 --> 00:13:31.061
a carbon-neutral energy system by the end of 2029.

00:13:31.741 --> 00:13:36.761
Renewables, factory waste heat and biogas have cut energy-related carbon emissions there

00:13:36.761 --> 00:13:38.501
by 79%.

00:13:38.501 --> 00:13:45.641
Two plants, glansager and cavars, take about 850,000 tons of organic material a year and

00:13:45.641 --> 00:13:47.461
cover the region's whole gas demand.

00:13:47.461 --> 00:13:53.461
In 2030, Denmark will be the first country to tax farm emissions, about 16 euros per

00:13:53.461 --> 00:13:54.781
ton of carbon dioxide.

00:13:55.281 --> 00:14:00.441
Jacob Sorensen of NOAA Friends of the Earth, Denmark, says this props up factory farming

00:14:00.441 --> 00:14:06.121
and locks pollution in, and that the money would do more on wind, solar, geothermal heat,

00:14:06.381 --> 00:14:07.281
and saving energy.

00:14:07.921 --> 00:14:13.581
Biogas Denmark says the gas deals with emissions the farms will produce anyway, and that those

00:14:13.581 --> 00:14:15.881
emissions become a bill once the tax starts.

00:14:16.501 --> 00:14:22.481
Project Zero's chief, Alan Pilgard Jensen, told Al Jazeera the point is climate and local

00:14:22.481 --> 00:14:26.561
supply when oil and gas swing because of the wars in Ukraine and Iran.

00:14:27.581 --> 00:14:30.001
Sorenson's complication sits on the same numbers.

00:14:30.561 --> 00:14:35.641
Most of the feedstock is manure, so the biogas business has a reason to keep the herd large.

00:14:36.567 --> 00:14:41.767
Nvidia formed a board committee to watch national security and export controls after Jensen

00:14:41.767 --> 00:14:46.867
Huang resigned over an affair with a woman US official suspect worked for Chinese intelligence.

00:14:47.687 --> 00:14:52.707
Mongolia's president, Kural Suk, said he will resign over claims he profited from

00:14:52.707 --> 00:14:55.807
a government railway and said the accusation is false.

00:14:56.487 --> 00:15:00.847
Our reign said it stopped a drone attack that Iran's revolutionary guard said targeted

